+Source: the thread "Extract morphometrics from gold tier 3 CT", 2026-10-30. The two morphometry sets (`morphometry enhance`, job 40872077, and `morphometry verse`, job 40877151) write long rows of a study, a level, a measure and a value, and the sex and age analysis needs each person's sex and age beside them, which no committed file holds. The join is one CPU job, the gate word `morphometry covariates` (grid/morphometry-covariates.sbatch, tools/gold3_covariates.py), on the owner's count; it ran once, job 40878978, which ended 0 on 2026-10-30 at 13:14 UTC over the rows of both sets as bordercall 16f7b40 measured them (code stamp 81e732f142d3aa16). On 2026-10-30 at 14:33 UTC the owner chose three jobs more ("Three: enhance, verse, covariates"): each set measured once more on the merged engine, bordercall ee495d5 (code stamp a56adf14a9e98b15), the first runs' reports and rows kept under their jobs (MORPHOMETRY_RERUNS in grid/gate.sh), then the join once more (COVARIATES_RERUNS), refused while either set's rerun is still to run. It waits for both sets' reports to end with exit 0 and for the census job's autoPET map, the newest whole sample index, VerSeFusion's demographics table and TotalSegmentator's meta.csv, and is refused, spending nothing, where the gate cannot read the checkout's commit or the commit lacks what the job copies from it. It runs from git's copy of its code at that commit; its interpreter is the SPINEPS environment's, as the morphometry sets' is, then the system's, and the checkout's train-cpu environment, which reads the working tree, only where none of those imports numpy and sqlite3 on Python 3.8 or later, the report naming which. A second job, for a job that left no report or a submission whose answer was lost, needs the owner's word in COVARIATES_RERUNS, one word a job, each lost answer its own (lost, lost2 and on).
+
+What the rerun changes and how it is guarded, from the reviews of the merged engine of 2026-10-30 (its consumers and its run time, both on phantoms in the thread's container, none on the grid's masks). Of the 31 measures the join prints, the merged engine reads 12 anew: pedicle_w, pedicle_h, pedicle_area, pedicle_chord, both pedicle angles, interpedicular, the four disc heights and foramen_h; the other 19 come from code the pin left alone. The rerun's lines for those 12 therefore supersede job 40878978's, and nothing off the grid should pool the two. The merged engine leaves pedicle_angle_sagittal unread where the posterior wall is not read or the slices leave the pedicle's climb loose, where the old one wrote 0.0, and on the review's phantoms it left the angle unread at every level of a 2.5 mm scan; since autoPET's CTs are cut at 3 mm in 821 of its 1014 rows of data/gold3-ct/enhance-pet/ct-details.json (2 mm in 141, 1 mm in 52), autoPET's pedicle_angle_sagittal cells are expected to rest mostly on its thinner scans, a subset chosen by scanner protocol. interpedicular is now read on the pedicles' medial walls, with the hole's width through its middle standing in, flagged interpedicular_band, where a pedicle is missing on a side; the join leaves those stand-ins out and counts them. Each set's job holds its joined rows to its code stamp and to its own count of the studies it chose, since a run whose worker died ends 0 with whatever files it found, and fails a set whose rows are not a whole run; the gate refuses the join while the two sets' reports name different code stamps, and the join's report names the stamp of the rows it joined. A join after the first is checked against every earlier one whose report printed cells: the gate hands the job their jobs (COVARIATES_PREVIOUS) and refuses, spending nothing, where one's joined.csv is gone, and the tool withholds each block where the two joins' persons or readings differ by 1 to 4 for a mean and SD, or 1 to 9 for r or a slope, so no two reports difference into one person's value. The set's folder is the next job's, so a report the gate sets aside for a rerun ends with a line saying where the files it names are now, and the verse rerun counts TotalSegmentator's subjects whose stacks job 40877151 made apart from those it stacks itself, since those stacks stay where they are and their lines are in that job's int16.log. A report that failed waits for the owner's word as one that ended 0 does, and a submission whose answer was lost holds every morphometry word while Slurm holds its job, found by its name or by the part it writes.
 
 Where each person and their sex and age come from, as the tool's docstring gives in full: autoPET's studies by the census's PETCT keys, one study a person (the first, the youngest age the index reads), sex and age from the DICOM headers in the sample index, whose fill rate is not recorded and which the report counts; Leipzig's and Careggi's studies carry no person id, sex or age anywhere, so each is its own person with sex unknown, counted in the fill rates and entering no table; VerSe's series by series.json's patient, sex from VerSeFusion's configs/verse_demographics.csv (sha256 in series.json), whose sex column's name is recorded nowhere, so the job reads the header, takes the one column named sex or gender and says a failure where there is none; TotalSegmentator's subjects from the release's semicolon-separated meta.csv (sha256 in subjects.json), extracted or inside the zip, whose ages the release jitters by up to four years, which flattens a slope a little. Left out: what the admission does not admit, ENHANCE.PET 1134, 1283 and 1347 (admitted on repaired masks but measured on the published ones) and the one ENHANCE.PET CT the census found off its mask's grid, found again by the job; an age above 110 is unknown (s1774, s1776 and s1839 read 115 to 118). The tables are of adults: a person whose age at the chosen study is under 18 enters none of them, no mean, g, correlation or slope, as docs/research/morphometry-beyond-the-42-papers.md recommends until the owner sets the age range, though the dataset itself still carries and flags every child (decision 13 below); a person of unknown age enters the sex tables but no age slope, which is over adults of known age alone, and the fill rates count the children and the persons of unknown age apart.
 
